## 7. Required modules and first-class pages

Build the following five fully realized core pages first. Every visible control must have a working local prototype behavior.

### A. ARSY DECK — Command Center
Headline: **THE WORK NEVER STOPS.**
Show clearly labeled demo metrics for active products, pipeline, marketplace readiness, gross receipts, net contribution, active agents, and experiments. Include Business Pulse, Opportunity Radar, Production Pipeline, AI Workforce, Channel Health, Activity Feed, and AFTERSHOCK insights. Never present demo revenue as real.

### B. SIGNAL ROOM — Market Intelligence
Headline: **READ THE SIGNAL.**
Show trend and category discovery, source stream, keyword observations, buyer problems, marketplace observations, seasonal radar, evidence dates, source links, confidence, and research status. Distinguish sourced evidence from hypotheses and model-generated synthesis. No invented search volumes or competitor sales.

### C. RIOT RADAR — Opportunity Lab
Provide opportunity detail: buyer problem, source evidence, demand signals, competition gap, product differentiation, channel suitability, unit economics assumptions, production complexity, policy gate, confidence, and recommendation. Include Go / Research More / Reject actions. A policy hard-stop cannot be overridden by a high score.

### D. THE FORGE — Product Workshop
Support the product families defined in docs/06-product-factories.md. Show creative brief, formats, generated preview placeholders, version, source assets, model/tool provenance, assigned specialist, production state, quality state, and distribution package. Use original demo artwork and coherent assets.

### E. ZILL WATCH — Quality & Integrity
Show IP/licensing, source provenance, similarity, technical specifications, completeness, metadata, platform disclosures, and policy checks. States: PASS, WARNING, BLOCKED, NEEDS REVIEW. Explain every finding. Policy violations are hard blocks, not just score deductions.

### Secondary modules
Create useful, consistent pages or clearly scoped previews for:
- LAUNCH BAY — channel capability, listing prep, manual package, official API, publication history.
- SIDRA ARCHIVE — asset catalog, versions, licenses, provenance.
- MIZAN LEDGER — gross, fees, refunds, variable cost, tax reserve, net contribution, payout.
- AFTERSHOCK — discovery, conversion, product lifetime, cohort and portfolio learning.
- RIOT ENGINE — specialist agents, runs, schedules, budgets, queue, approvals, logs.
- SETTINGS / POLICY CENTER — country, timezone, currencies, platform eligibility checks, credentials placeholders, consent, data controls, policy review dates.

## 8. Business truth and marketplace boundaries

Marketplace names must be treated as candidate channels, not verified live connections.

Show connection states honestly:
- NOT CONNECTED
- ELIGIBILITY CHECK REQUIRED
- MANUAL WORKFLOW
- OFFICIAL API AVAILABLE (only when verified for the exact action)
- LIMITED OFFICIAL INTEGRATION
- PAUSED / POLICY REVIEW

Never imply KDP, Adobe Stock, Etsy, Gumroad, Shopee, TikTok Shop, YouTube, Roblox, or itch.io is connected or publishing successfully in the demo.

No fake transactions, fake reviews, artificial downloads, engagement manipulation, scraping behind login, CAPTCHA bypass, rate-limit evasion, or undisclosed automated posting.

The product's promise is reduced repetitive work and evidence-based portfolio decisions—not guaranteed income or zero owner responsibility.

